<p>Chapter 2 told you what utilitarianism is. Chapter 3 asks why anyone is motivated to act on it, and Chapter 4 tries to prove the principle itself. Mill's proof is widely regarded as one of the most famous errors in moral philosophy, and we will spend some time on exactly where it goes wrong.</p>
